# Applied on top of Microsoft/config-wsl of the pinned microsoft/WSL2-Linux-Kernel tag (see build.sh): what the Android
# container needs and the stock WSL2 kernel lacks. Everything else the guest needs (memfd, PSI, user namespaces, overlayfs,
# squashfs, dxgkrnl, vsock) is already on in the stock config. CONFIG_LOCALVERSION stays stock so the stock module
# VHD (iptables, tun, bridge) keeps loading.
CONFIG_ANDROID_BINDER_IPC=y
CONFIG_ANDROID_BINDERFS=y
CONFIG_ANDROID_BINDER_DEVICES=""
# Android system images are EROFS and the stock kernel only has it as a module.
CONFIG_EROFS_FS=y
